  "reflectionText": "Paul wrote: we have this treasure in clay vessels, that the surpassing greatness of the power may be of God. Pressed but not crushed. Perplexed but not despairing. Struck down but not destroyed. The outward man decays; the inward man is renewed day by day. What does it feel like to carry the treasure in the very clay that is wearing thin?"
